## Settings

All settings of `mowdeck-service-kit` apply (`MOWDECK_*`, any value also from `MOWDECK_<NAME>_FILE`). Service specific settings and changed defaults:

| Variable | Default | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `MOWDECK_SERVICE_NAME` | `{{ service_name }}` | Service name in logs, metrics and traces |
| `MOWDECK_HTTP_PORT` | `{{ http_port }}` | HTTP port |
{%- if needs_db %}
| `MOWDECK_DATABASE_URL` | unset | PostgreSQL URL (usually `MOWDECK_DATABASE_URL_FILE`); the database is not used when unset |
{%- endif %}

## Layers

| Package | Content | Rule |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `domain/` | models and rules | pure Python, no I/O, no framework imports |
| `application/` | use cases and ports (`Protocol`s) | depends on `domain` and ports only |
| `adapters/api/` | FastAPI routers | translate HTTP to use cases, check permissions |
| `adapters/bus/` | NATS subscriptions and publishers | translate messages to use cases |
{%- if needs_db %}
| `adapters/db/` | SQLAlchemy engine, Alembic migrations | implement repository ports |
{%- endif %}
| `main.py` | wiring (`build_app`) and `main()` | the only place that knows every layer |

## Local start

```bash
uv sync
docker compose -f infra/compose/docker-compose.yml up -d --wait nats{% if needs_db %} postgres{% endif %}
{%- if needs_db %}
MOWDECK_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://{{ package_name }}:<password>@127.0.0.1:5432/{{ package_name }} \
  uv run python -m {{ package_name }}.adapters.db.migrate
{%- endif %}
MOWDECK_ENVIRONMENT=dev uv run python -m {{ package_name }}.main
curl http://127.0.0.1:{{ http_port }}/readyz
```

Container image (build context is the repository root):

```bash
docker build -f services/{{ service_name }}/Dockerfile -t mowdeck/{{ service_name }}:dev .
```

The Compose block is in `compose.snippet.yml`; for Kubernetes add a template to the umbrella chart `infra/helm/mowdeck` (see `docs/ops/helm.md`).
{%- if needs_db %}

## Migrations

Migrations run as a separate step before the service starts (Compose: `{{ service_name }}-migrate`, Helm: a Job), never inside the service process. They must stay backward compatible for rolling updates.

```bash
uv run alembic -c services/{{ service_name }}/alembic.ini revision -m "add table"   # new revision
uv run python -m {{ package_name }}.adapters.db.migrate                            # upgrade head
```
{%- endif %}

